# SYNOPSIS

```usage
/lib/ld-vx
```

# DESCRIPTION

`ld-vx` starts a dynamic program, one whose ELF image names `/lib/ld-vx` as its interpreter (`PT_INTERP`, ADR-0047).
It is never run by name: a spawn (svcd(8), rc(1)) that is asked for such a program reads the interpreter from its own namespace, or svcd from the boot image, maps it in the program's place, and gives it the program's image as the handle `dl.exe`.

`ld-vx` builds the namespace from the spawn message, as any program does, then:

- maps the program at the addresses it was linked for;
- maps each library its `DT_NEEDED` entries name, and theirs, breadth first and each once, from `/lib/NAME` in that namespace, with no search path (so a dynamic program needs a namespace with `/lib` in it: a manifest with no `ns=` gives none); each library at a random base inside a reservation of its span, with a page left unmapped on each side;
- binds every symbol before the program runs, the first definition in that order winning, the program's own first; there is no lazy binding and no interposition;
- makes each object's RELRO read-only;
- lays out the objects' thread-local storage one after another, the program's where its linker put it;
- and jumps to the program's entry with the handover (`abi/vx/dl.h`): the spawn message as it read it, with its handles, and the loaded objects.

The program's vx-rt then lays out each thread's TLS from every object, runs the libraries' constructors before its own, a library's dependencies first, and their destructors after its own, in reverse; it keeps the list of objects for the unwinder and dbg(1).

A library is linked `-shared` with `-fPIC` and the initial-exec TLS model, `-z now` and `-z relro`; a dynamic program with `--dynamic-linker=/lib/ld-vx`.
`./build` makes both (`LINK_SHARED`, `LINK_DYNAMIC` in its program table), and puts libraries in the boot image's `lib/`, which a namespace with the boot image as its root has at `/lib`.

# SEE ALSO

svcd(8), rc(1), native(7), image(2); ADR-0047 in the repository

# DIAGNOSTICS

A program that cannot be loaded ends with the exit string `ld-vx: NAME: why`: a library `/lib` does not have, an undefined symbol, a relocation of a kind it does not take, or an address outside the object that holds it.

# BUGS

Only the libraries a program needs at start are loaded; a program maps one later with `vx_image_open` (image(2)), which refuses one with TLS: dynamic TLS (`__tls_get_addr`, TLS descriptors) is not implemented.
Its own pages stay mapped for the life of the process.
svcd(8), rc(1), dbg(1) and the POSIX personality's `posix_spawn` and `exec` give a program its interpreter; relays start a static program. A POSIX program's interpreter is musl's `libc.so`, `/lib/ld-musl-`<arch>`.so.1` (posix(7)), which takes the same `dl.exe` but none of this handover. dbg(1) cannot yet set a breakpoint in a dynamic program before it runs: its executable is mapped by its interpreter.
